# Everything in this repository is checked out and committed with LF.
#
# Development happens on Windows but CI, hassfest, the HACS action and Home Assistant itself all
# run on Linux. Two of the checks are byte-exact and would fail on line endings alone: the
# strings.json <-> translations/en.json `diff`, and `ruff format --check`. Normalising here means
# the working copy matches what CI sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
